\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Glorious master, Lord Almighty,
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0   It is Thou that I am calling,
\par   I, begotten of earth,
\par   Undeserving, by all standards,
\par   And given unto life and death,
\par   Transgressor and orphan.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Lo, I stand on a mighty rock,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Torn between two mighty oceans,
\par In utter confusion.
\par When the time appointed is due,
\par It is unto God I shall go,
\par Or into the fiery hell.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  O my Lord, God change thou my thoughts;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 And Thy acts of lasting goodness,
\par Have them planted in my heart.
\par Make me know its worthwhile value,
\par So that I may strive to possess,
\par And never retire to rot!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. When Thou cometh in Thy glory,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 On the day appointed for such,
\par Clothe me in Thy raiment.
\par Teach me to offer Thee worship
\par When you judge the nations on earth;
\par That I am not judged as well.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. May this be my thought ev'ryday,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj That the life eternal I'll find,
\par Making every effort,
\par What Thou ordained has come to pass,
\par Come and have me filled each new day,
\par With Thy acts of holiness.\tab 
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  Be merciful to me O Lord,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Grant my soul your life eternal,
\par That it shall live with Thee!
\par There shall faith be terminated
\par And hope receive its due ending,
\par \pard        In an everlasting love!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

